s are preserved (no NAT) both before and after a full one-at-a-time restart of all three nodes. The mandatory restart evidence protocol was executed thoroughly and is corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. The only blemish is two small log files left behind in /tmp on node3 after a cleanup command was cut short.","limitations":["Reachability and port-forwarding were only tested with ICMP and two specific TCP ports (5555, 6666); no firewall/ACL restricting other ports was observed, so 'any port' is inferred from the absence of filtering rather than exhaustively tested against every port/protocol.","The final cleanup command on node3 (cmd-c7643e5b096c496c) terminated with return_code 143 before completing, leaving two temporary files (/tmp/tdump2.log, /tmp/nc_out2.log) as directly observed in the after_executor snapshot."]},"ttft_ms":26569,"type":"result","duration_ms":73030,"uuid":"b90ecae3-4760-472e-96ee-9cb319c6874b","ttft_stream_ms":2405,"time_to_request_ms":43,"queued_turn_count":0}
